  "bbox": [
   2212,
   1215,
   2494,
   1274
  ],
  "angle": 4.4,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "The verifier answers with a price — or rejects with a reason — see HOW THE VERIFIER ANSWERS",
  "role": "body",
  "bbox": [
   2232,
   1282,
   2482,
   1399
  ],
  "angle": 4.6,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "The issuer decides what to do with that answer — see THE ISSUER'S CHOICE",
  "role": "body",
  "bbox": [
   2215,
   1396,
   2468,
   1473
  ],
  "angle": 4.6,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "Each retry adds to the cost — as shown earlier on PUBLISHING COST",
  "role": "body",
  "bbox": [
   2208,
   1479,
   2449,
   1568
  ],
  "angle": 4.9,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "THE ALGORITHM PICKS — YOU DO NOT.",
  "role": "tagline",
  "bbox": [
   1312,
   1585,
   2499,
   1681
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "CAN YOU BRUTE-FORCE IT?",
  "role": "label",
  "bbox": [
   96,
   1015,
   447,
   1064
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "I could grind thousands of drafts until one lands on the verifier I want…",
  "role": "body",
  "bbox": [
   268,
   1065,
   667,
   1127
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "the hash is deterministic but pre-image-resistant — each small edit throws the pick somewhere unrelated.",
  "role": "caption",
  "bbox": [
   58,
   1285,
   643,
   1349
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "BUT THE AUTHORITY SEALS THE REST",
  "role": "label",
  "bbox": [
   101,
   1353,
   590,
   1399
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "AUTHORITY-SIGNED EVIDENCE ABOUT OTHERS",
  "role": "label",
  "bbox": [
   251,
   1402,
   526,
   1468
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "…but I cannot predict what the authority will sign — and I cannot tell whether she is in league with me or not.",
  "role": "body",
  "bbox": [
   543,
   1409,
   812,
   1543
  ],
  "angle": 0,
  "joined": false
 },
 {
  "text": "because the hash eats authority-signed evidence too, the issuer cannot forecast his own hash. For the community, the question becomes: do we trust this authority — and this issuer-with-this-authority — at all?",
